Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: derive PPS width from the current mode

DSC picture width is retained in mode-private state. On Neo3, the driver
generated a 3840-wide PPS while the DSC hardware and panel use a
1920-wide picture. Multiplying the stored width compounds the value
across repeated enables.

Derive the full picture width from the current per-controller mode each
time so repeated modesets cannot double it again.

--- a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_display.c
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_display.c
@@ -7603,6 +7603,7 @@ int dsi_display_enable(struct dsi_display *display)
 	if ((mode->priv_info->dsc_enabled) &&
 			!(mode->dsi_mode_flags & DSI_MODE_FLAG_DMS_FPS)) {
-		mode->priv_info->dsc.pic_width *= display->ctrl_count;
+		mode->priv_info->dsc.pic_width =
+			mode->timing.h_active * display->ctrl_count;
 		rc = dsi_panel_update_pps(display->panel);
 		if (rc) {
 			DSI_ERR("[%s] panel pps cmd update failed, rc=%d\n",
